WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.710 --> 00:00:05.330
- Hi, I'm Maeghan from Khan Academy.

00:00:05.330 --> 00:00:06.163
In this video,

00:00:06.163 --> 00:00:09.380
we'll learn how to find
and assign exercises,

00:00:09.380 --> 00:00:11.650
videos, and articles on Khan Academy

00:00:11.650 --> 00:00:13.593
for your classes or students.

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:17.870
In order to create an assignment,

00:00:17.870 --> 00:00:20.120
we recommend teachers start by finding

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:23.060
and assigning content right
from the assignments tab

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:24.910
on the teacher dashboard.

00:00:24.910 --> 00:00:26.650
From the teacher dashboard,

00:00:26.650 --> 00:00:28.403
select one of your classes,

00:00:28.403 --> 00:00:32.191
and then click on assignments
on the left side navigation

00:00:32.191 --> 00:00:35.890
to expand all of the
options under assignments,

00:00:35.890 --> 00:00:37.533
and then click assign.

00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:40.400
Now, select your preferred course

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:42.210
from the dropdown menu.

00:00:42.210 --> 00:00:43.800
You will see the full content

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:46.253
for the course divided into units.

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:49.566
Units are organized into lessons,

00:00:49.566 --> 00:00:54.566
which in turn contain videos,
articles, and exercises.

00:00:55.490 --> 00:00:57.100
Courses that are already aligned

00:00:57.100 --> 00:00:59.403
with the Common Core and AP

00:00:59.403 --> 00:01:02.820
show the standards tag to each unit,

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:07.453
lesson, video, article, and exercise.

00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:10.860
By clicking a piece of content,

00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:14.220
you can view the
exercise, watch the video,

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:17.573
or read the article before
assigning it to students.

00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:21.876
In addition, hovering
the cursor over a code

00:01:21.876 --> 00:01:24.903
shows the text of that
Common Core standard.

00:01:26.370 --> 00:01:28.050
When you find what you need,

00:01:28.050 --> 00:01:30.170
check the boxes for individual pieces

00:01:30.170 --> 00:01:32.970
of content or the entire lesson,

00:01:32.970 --> 00:01:34.513
and then click assign.

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:38.480
While it may seem appealing

00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:41.210
to assign an entire unit to a class,

00:01:41.210 --> 00:01:42.573
we don't recommend this.

00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:45.790
When you assign a unit to a class,

00:01:45.790 --> 00:01:48.663
each item appears as a separate
assignment to students,

00:01:49.530 --> 00:01:51.680
which means you could be giving students

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:54.843
20, 30, or even 60 assignments.

00:01:55.870 --> 00:01:57.980
Whenever you assign a piece of content,

00:01:57.980 --> 00:02:00.470
you need to choose the class or classes,

00:02:00.470 --> 00:02:04.293
students, due date, and
time of the assignments.

00:02:05.410 --> 00:02:07.720
You can assign to a specific class,

00:02:07.720 --> 00:02:08.860
a few classes,

00:02:08.860 --> 00:02:10.613
or all of your classes at once.

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:13.860
You can still assign for one student,

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:16.533
a group of students, or
all of your students.

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:20.880
There is also an option for teachers

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:23.510
to select the content they wish to assign,

00:02:23.510 --> 00:02:26.860
but save the assignment for
some time in the future.

00:02:26.860 --> 00:02:28.960
You can click assign
to send the assignment

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:30.460
to students immediately,

00:02:30.460 --> 00:02:32.110
or click save and assign later

00:02:32.110 --> 00:02:34.283
to save the assignments for a later time.

00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:37.550
In addition, for exercises,

00:02:37.550 --> 00:02:39.030
you can decide whether students

00:02:39.030 --> 00:02:41.900
will receive the same
question in the same order,

00:02:41.900 --> 00:02:43.940
or a set of questions selected at random

00:02:43.940 --> 00:02:45.993
from that exercises item bank.

00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:48.090
One note,

00:02:48.090 --> 00:02:49.990
you can always view the complete item bank

00:02:49.990 --> 00:02:53.510
for an exercise by
clicking the exercise name.

00:02:53.510 --> 00:02:55.580
Teachers share that viewing the item bank

00:02:55.580 --> 00:02:57.305
before creating an assignment

00:02:57.305 --> 00:03:00.400
helps them ensure they
are the right questions

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:02.250
and help some flag any concerns

00:03:02.250 --> 00:03:04.623
before assigning the content to students.

00:03:07.100 --> 00:03:08.920
In the case of classroom practice,

00:03:08.920 --> 00:03:10.930
the most common option is to ask students

00:03:10.930 --> 00:03:13.630
to work on the same set of questions.

00:03:13.630 --> 00:03:16.910
This allows you to quickly
identify common mistakes,

00:03:16.910 --> 00:03:19.210
which highlights areas for reteaching

00:03:19.210 --> 00:03:22.130
or allows you to quickly
identify common areas

00:03:22.130 --> 00:03:26.143
of success to provide
opportunities for celebration.

00:03:27.190 --> 00:03:28.830
If you are using assignments

00:03:28.830 --> 00:03:31.240
for independent practice or homework,

00:03:31.240 --> 00:03:32.800
many teachers prefer students

00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:35.130
to work on different questions.

00:03:35.130 --> 00:03:36.450
In these situations,

00:03:36.450 --> 00:03:38.910
students are given a consistent number,

00:03:38.910 --> 00:03:41.630
variety, and rigor of questions,

00:03:41.630 --> 00:03:43.832
but because the questions
are not identical,

00:03:43.832 --> 00:03:46.683
students are encouraged
to work independently.

00:03:48.750 --> 00:03:50.420
Another way to make assignments

00:03:50.420 --> 00:03:51.953
is through the skills report.

00:03:52.990 --> 00:03:55.172
The skills report shows
the level of skill mastery

00:03:55.172 --> 00:03:58.160
for every skill for every student,

00:03:58.160 --> 00:04:00.879
which makes it a valuable
tool for assigning content

00:04:00.879 --> 00:04:03.513
that meets the needs of each student.

00:04:05.540 --> 00:04:08.010
Select the unit to expand the report

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:11.460
and view all of the
skills within the unit.

00:04:11.460 --> 00:04:13.310
By hovering over the purple bar

00:04:13.310 --> 00:04:15.130
to the right of the skill name,

00:04:15.130 --> 00:04:17.360
you can get a quick view of the number

00:04:17.360 --> 00:04:20.320
of students at each skill level.

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:22.310
By clicking on the skill name,

00:04:22.310 --> 00:04:24.192
you can expand the view of the skill

00:04:24.192 --> 00:04:26.470
to see which students in the class

00:04:26.470 --> 00:04:28.713
are currently at each skill level.

00:04:29.750 --> 00:04:32.460
You can then use the
assign this skill button

00:04:32.460 --> 00:04:34.900
on the right hand side to assign the skill

00:04:34.900 --> 00:04:36.604
to an individual student,

00:04:36.604 --> 00:04:39.433
group of students, or all students.

00:04:42.050 --> 00:04:43.700
The same popup that appears

00:04:43.700 --> 00:04:46.203
in the assignment tab will appear here.

00:04:48.130 --> 00:04:50.040
You can preview the types of questions

00:04:50.040 --> 00:04:52.050
that are included in this exercise

00:04:52.050 --> 00:04:55.183
by hovering over the
blue view exercise link.

00:04:57.450 --> 00:04:59.130
Clicking on the link will take you

00:04:59.130 --> 00:05:01.843
to the student view of the same exercise.

00:05:02.840 --> 00:05:06.270
Many teachers suggest using
this report to assign skills

00:05:06.270 --> 00:05:08.020
the students at the not started

00:05:08.020 --> 00:05:10.440
or attempted levels to encourage them

00:05:10.440 --> 00:05:14.030
to increase their practice
time on that skill.

00:05:14.030 --> 00:05:15.600
Another way to make assignments

00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:18.600
on Khan Academy is through the toolbar.

00:05:18.600 --> 00:05:20.980
When you browse any
content on Khan Academy

00:05:20.980 --> 00:05:22.930
from the student perspective,

00:05:22.930 --> 00:05:25.690
as long as you are logged
into your teacher account,

00:05:25.690 --> 00:05:29.010
the toolbar will appear
at the top of the page.

00:05:29.010 --> 00:05:31.150
You can use the toolbar
to make assignments

00:05:31.150 --> 00:05:32.940
using the same information you would

00:05:32.940 --> 00:05:35.423
from the assignments tab or skills report.

00:05:36.310 --> 00:05:38.210
One other thing.

00:05:38.210 --> 00:05:40.280
You can also find the content you need

00:05:40.280 --> 00:05:42.110
by using the search bar.

00:05:42.110 --> 00:05:43.876
You can search by subject,

00:05:43.876 --> 00:05:47.600
concept, or even by standards.

00:05:47.600 --> 00:05:50.719
Common Core state standards
for K through 12 math

00:05:50.719 --> 00:05:54.850
or AP standards for our AP courses.

00:05:54.850 --> 00:05:58.090
You can then filter the results by videos,

00:05:58.090 --> 00:06:01.273
articles, exercises, and more.

00:06:02.154 --> 00:06:03.950
When you find the content you want,

00:06:03.950 --> 00:06:06.080
click on the item and use the tool bar

00:06:06.080 --> 00:06:08.173
to complete the assignment options.

00:06:09.590 --> 00:06:12.764
If you ever need to edit
or delete an assignment,

00:06:12.764 --> 00:06:16.203
use the manage tab under assignments.

00:06:19.710 --> 00:06:22.624
Now that you have an idea of
how to create assignments,

00:06:22.624 --> 00:06:24.820
a question we hear a lot is

00:06:24.820 --> 00:06:26.823
what does this look like for students?

00:06:28.180 --> 00:06:31.560
Students will find assignments
on their learner home page,

00:06:31.560 --> 00:06:34.620
the page they see as soon as they log in,

00:06:34.620 --> 00:06:37.463
under the assignments tab for each class.

00:06:38.720 --> 00:06:41.980
Students will see all of
their active assignments,

00:06:41.980 --> 00:06:43.200
past assignments,

00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:45.753
and the due dates for
completing each assignment.

00:06:47.770 --> 00:06:49.624
Assignments are organized by due date

00:06:49.624 --> 00:06:52.930
with the soonest due date at the top.

00:06:52.930 --> 00:06:54.784
As students complete their assignments

00:06:54.784 --> 00:06:57.300
and work on each question,

00:06:57.300 --> 00:07:00.550
they receive instant feedback
on how they are doing,

00:07:00.550 --> 00:07:02.420
and both you and the student receive data

00:07:02.420 --> 00:07:05.263
on their performance
almost instantaneously.

00:07:06.780 --> 00:07:09.020
Students are enabled to
make several attempts

00:07:09.020 --> 00:07:11.350
to complete the assignments,

00:07:11.350 --> 00:07:14.483
and we encourage students to
learn from their own mistakes.

00:07:15.590 --> 00:07:18.870
If you assign different
questions for each student,

00:07:18.870 --> 00:07:21.530
they will receive a new
set of questions selected

00:07:21.530 --> 00:07:24.300
at random on each attempt.

00:07:24.300 --> 00:07:25.920
And just as a reminder,

00:07:25.920 --> 00:07:29.270
students can also view
and complete assignments

00:07:29.270 --> 00:07:32.203
for any class in the
Khan Academy mobile app.

00:07:33.310 --> 00:07:35.880
We know this is a lot of
information to take in,

00:07:35.880 --> 00:07:37.780
and we hope this helps you as teachers

00:07:37.780 --> 00:07:41.350
to create assignments for
your students on Khan Academy.

00:07:41.350 --> 00:07:45.190
Some concepts work particularly
well for classroom practice.

00:07:45.190 --> 00:07:47.060
Choose concepts that are more difficult

00:07:47.060 --> 00:07:50.820
or that can generate good
discussions and debates.

00:07:50.820 --> 00:07:52.500
Start slowly by creating just

00:07:52.500 --> 00:07:55.060
a few assignments to do in a class.

00:07:55.060 --> 00:07:58.970
Most teachers recommend three
to five assignments per week.

00:07:58.970 --> 00:08:01.808
Gradually, you will build up a
routine of using Khan Academy

00:08:01.808 --> 00:08:04.880
that best meets the pace of your students.

00:08:04.880 --> 00:08:06.710
We hope this video helps you

00:08:06.710 --> 00:08:08.350
get started creating assignments

00:08:08.350 --> 00:08:10.393
for your students on Khan Academy.

